   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Status of Implementation Progress: Output 1:

a. Completed. Policy Action 2: To increase financial resources for post-primary

education, government increased secondary education block grants to

KN70,000 per student (from KN50,000 per student) and increased TVET

block grants to KN300,000 per student (from KN270,000).

b. Completed. Policy Action 1: To strengthen post-primary education planning and

budgeting and align it better to labor demand, MOES issued an instruction requiring relevant education departments to prepare action plans for secondary education, TVET and higher education, emphasizing gender equity.

c. On track to meet target. The Project has developed a series of trainings and workshops to support MOES strengthen the LESMIS system and build staff capacity for managing an integrated system for post-primary education. If the COVID-19 restrictions persist, these will need to be held online. A manual on data analysis has been drafted. The ESSC has updated the LESMIS to produce current data at school, district, provincial and national levels.

d. On track to meet target. The project has confirmed the clustering of schools for the pilot and proposed two partnering models: (i) summer courses, and (ii) curriculum integration. The Project will review the approach for the pilot and determine an appropriate annual budget for the pilot to ensure sustainability. Given limited budget for its implementation, the EA will draft a comprehensive plan and revised budget for this pilot.

Output 2

a. Completed. Policy Action 3: To increase quality of teaching across schools, MOES

issued improved standards for textbooks, teacher guides and instructional materials for general education (including secondary education), mainstreaming sensitivity to gender, ethnic groups and those with disabilities.

Completed. Policy Action 6: To support continuing professional development programs for lower and upper secondary education teachers (including

teachers of science, mathematics, English and Lao language), MOES trained more secondary pedagogical advisers.

b. Completed. Policy Action 4: To improve training standards, MOES accredited eight provincial/regional teacher training institutions to provide quality teacher training at bachelor level in specific subject majors including lower and upper secondary level sciences, mathematics and Lao language.

c. Completed. Policy Action 5: To enhance learning outcomes, MOES introduced

learner-centered pedagogy for general education schools (including secondary education schools).

d. On track to meet target. Teacher training to pilot the teacher guides with teachers, school leadership, pedagogical advisors and core master trainers is expected to start in August 2021. The Project is also piloting synchronous learning in live-online trainings with asynchronous self-learning components after the webinars with online assessments.

e. On track to meet target.

f. On track to meet target. The Project is working closely with the Research Institute for Educational Sciences (RIES) and the Department of Teacher Education on the curriculum reform and teacher training development as well as coordinating with the BEQUAL program funded by Australia to support the primary education curriculum.

g. On track to meet target. Teacher training to pilot the teacher guides with teachers, school leadership, pedagogical advisors and core master trainers is expected to start in August 2021. The Project is also piloting synchronous learning in live-online trainings with asynchronous self-learning components after the webinars with online assessments.

h. On track to meet target. The Project plans to prepare detailed teacher guides to support teachers in the classroom and in their schools post-trainings. Teacher training to pilot the teacher guides with teachers, school leadership, pedagogical advisors and core master trainers is expected to start in August 2021.

i. On track to meet target. Initial procurement to start in Q4 2021.

Output 3:

a. Completed. Policy Action 7: To improve tracking of learning outcomes, MOES instructed departments to revise the Assessment Framework for General

Education (including secondary education).

